    '**HANDOVER · international capacity and interconnect · L. Saad to R. Nasr · effective 12 November · read before our hour on Monday at 09.00**',
    '**HOW THIS NOTE IS ORGANISED, AND WHY.** **By decision, not by topic.** **The passwords, the rota, the provider list and the contract folder are in the shared drive and you can read them without me.** **What you cannot read is why nine things are the way they are, and that is what follows: each with the date it was decided, the reason, and what would make it worth changing.** **Without the last part you inherit nine rules and no way out of any of them.**',
    '**THE DECISIONS, WITH THEIR CONDITIONS FOR REVISITING.** **The Cyprus provider is paid quarterly, not monthly: imposed July 2023 after two disputed settlements; revisit if they are clean for eight consecutive quarters — they are at five.** **The Sednaya teleport is never left unmanned on a Friday: decided 2022 after a feed failed during a live transmission; revisit when the remote monitoring is commissioned, due in June.** **Transit traffic is not routed through Amman Link between 22.00 and 02.00: decided after the fraud of March; revisit when their fraud reporting is automated, which they have promised twice.**',
    '**THE PEOPLE, AND I HAVE WRITTEN ONLY WHAT HAPPENS.** **The night engineer will not telephone a manager after midnight unless he has been told explicitly that he may — two outages went unreported until 06.00 before the standing instruction was written.** **Hala Deeb holds every settlement definition in her head and has written one of them down; that is the next handover problem after this one and I have not solved it.** **Nothing else here is an opinion about anybody and you should not read one into it.**',
    '**WHAT IS ABOUT TO HAPPEN, WITH DATES.** **The Cyprus interconnect renews on 1 September unless notice is given by 1 July.** **The superseded availability report of 2 April is still in the board pack and is not marked — I have marked our copy and you should remove it rather than trust the marking.** **The Nordwave support contract ends 30 April and should go out to two others this time.**',
