  wModel: { title: 'an application', lines: [
    '**APPLICATION · commercial manager, international · from 1 January · L. Saad, corporate accounts and capacity · 11 November**',
    '**WHY I AM WRITING, IN ONE SENTENCE.** **I apply for the post of commercial manager, international, from 1 January, on the strength of four years in which international settlement disputes fell from six a year to one and the transit relationship grew from 140 to 180 million pounds a year.** **Both figures are in the quarterly settlement returns, which H. Deeb compiles and I have not calculated for this letter.**',
    '**THREE THINGS I DECIDED, AND WHAT EACH CHANGED.** **The Cyprus settlement moved to quarterly after two disputed quarters in 2023: disputes fell from two a year to none in eight quarters and the change cost nothing in cash.** **Transit routing through Amman Link suspended between 22.00 and 02.00 after the March fraud: the loss stopped that night and has not recurred in fourteen months.** **The interconnect definition register started in 2023 — nine carriers, one definition each, two of them now signed: it is the only reason the March settlement question was answered in a week rather than five months.**',
    '**WHAT I GOT WRONG, AND WHAT I DID ABOUT IT.** **I recommended the Zhongtai third-party support arrangement for a year after the vendor had twice refused verbally to warrant it, and I never asked them in writing.** **It cost about 9 million pounds and one failed commissioning.** **Since then nothing goes into a recommendation of mine unless the counterparty has confirmed it in writing, which has held for two years and has twice slowed a decision by a fortnight.** **I include it because an application at this level with no mistake in it tells a reader either that the candidate has not done enough to make one or that something has been left out.**',
    '**THE GAP, NAMED BY ME.** **I have never managed a capital budget and I have never chaired a board item.** **I have written two board papers and sat behind the director at one review, and preparing a paper is not answering a board.** **I would want three months’ sight of the capital plan alongside whoever holds it, and to take one board item with the director in the room before I take one alone.**',
    '**NINETY DAYS, AND A NAME BESIDE EVERY CLAIM.** **One: the nine interconnect definitions signed rather than seven unsigned.** **Two: the unwritten-knowledge list in my handover note closed, with an owner against each item.** **Three: a fortnight finding out how the dealer channel actually prices, because I do not know.** **And the witnesses: settlement figures — H. Deeb; the fraud suspension — O. Sabbagh and the March file; the definition register — the register itself; the Zhongtai recommendation and its cost — T. Mansour, who warned me at the time and whose warning is in the file.** **Two sentences came out of this letter because I could not name anybody for them.**' ] },
